-- An author-written ASSUME that shares a name with its own section's GIVEN.
-- L4 resolves names by type, so the two bindings coexist and the file checks
-- clean: `label` reads the STRING one, `doubled` the NUMBER one.
--
-- The checker tells the section GIVEN's own elaboration (a 0-ary ASSUME it
-- prepends for `income`) apart from this ASSUME by identity — the elaboration
-- carries no tokens — and not by name alone. Measured 2026-09-07 before that
-- repair (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.1.2): the name-only test took this
-- ASSUME for the checker's own, so it drew no deprecation warning and was
-- dropped from the re-printed module. Exactly one warning is expected here,
-- on line 13, and `l4 batch`'s re-print must keep the declaration.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN income IS A NUMBER

ASSUME income IS A STRING

GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `label` IS income

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `doubled` IS income TIMES 2

#CHECK `label`
#CHECK `doubled`
